23. FINAL STATEMENT

This task demonstrated the complete machine learning workflow for a restaurant rating prediction problem, from exploratory data analysis and preprocessing to feature engineering, target leakage prevention, model training, evaluation, comparison, error analysis, feature interpretation, and documentation.

The final Random Forest Regression model provided the strongest performance among the evaluated approaches and demonstrated the effectiveness of machine learning for predicting restaurant ratings from the available restaurant attributes.